.git/
release/
logs.*
*.pdf
*.mp4
*.tiff
db4/
autom4te.cache/
configure
config.log
config.status
# Build hygiene: the daemon image (C++ only) needs none of these; excluding them
# keeps the build context small (.cache holds multi-GB chain data + backups).
.cache/
newUI/
release_test/
**/node_modules/
*.log
*.zip
*.tar.gz
# Build artifacts: the Dockerfile runs a fresh autogen+configure+make, so copying
# stale host objects/binaries in would risk make skipping a recompile (wrong binary)
# and bloats the context. Force a clean compile.
#
# The tree also carries leftover MinGW cross-compile output ("Intel amd64 COFF
# object file"). Mixing that into a Linux link produces
#   undefined reference to `operator new(unsigned long long)'   <- Win64 mangling
#   BFD assertion fail ../../bfd/reloc.c / dangerous relocation
#   collect2: fatal error: ld terminated with signal 11
# The extension patterns below match at every depth, which is what removes them.
#
# Do NOT add ".libs/" or "**/.libs/": libtool CREATES those directories during
# the in-container build, and excluding the path makes the link fail with
# "cannot find univalue/.libs/libunivalue.a: No such file or directory".
*.o
*.a
*.lo
*.la
*.Po
*.exe
*.dll
# Prebuilt cross-compile dependency trees. depends/x86_64-w64-mingw32/ holds a
# full Win64 toolchain output (OpenSSL, boost, ...); configure picks it up and
# the Linux link then dies on Windows-only symbols:
#   undefined reference to `__imp_RtlVirtualUnwind'
# The Dockerfile builds its own deps from apt, so none of depends/ is needed.
depends/x86_64-w64-mingw32/
depends/x86_64-apple-darwin*/
depends/work/
depends/built/
depends/sources/
src/phicoind
src/phicoin-cli
src/phicoin-tx
src/qt/phicoin-qt
src/test/test_phicoin
src/bench/bench_phicoin
